## PHASE 1.1: BLACK FORMATTING (Idempotent)

```bash
cd ~/dutchbay-epc-model

echo "=== BLACK FORMATTING PASS 1 ==="
.venv311/bin/python -m black \
  analytics/ \
  finance/ \
  tests/ \
  scripts/ \
  run_full_pipeline.py \
  --line-length 88 \
  --target-version py311

# This should complete with "N files left unchanged" or small number of reformatted
# If Black hangs on any file, Ctrl+C and investigate that file
```

**Expected Output:**
```
All done! X file(s) would be reformatted, Y file(s) left unchanged.
```

---

## PHASE 1.2: AUTO-REMOVE UNUSED IMPORTS

```bash
cd ~/dutchbay-epc-model

echo "=== AUTOFLAKE: REMOVE UNUSED IMPORTS ==="

# Run autoflake with review-first approach
.venv311/bin/python -m autoflake \
  --remove-all-unused-imports \
  --recursive \
  --in-place \
  --exclude=analytics/fx/,scripts/research/,scripts/test_fx_*.py \
  analytics/ finance/ tests/ scripts/ \
  run_full_pipeline.py

# Check what changed
echo ""
echo "=== CHANGES FROM AUTOFLAKE ==="
git diff --stat

# Review key changes (imports only)
git diff --name-only | head -10 | xargs -I {} sh -c 'echo "=== {} ==="; git diff {} | head -20'
```

**Note:** `--exclude` skips FX and research (we're deferring those). This prevents accidentally removing "unused" imports that are actually used in those modules.

---

## PHASE 1.3: FIX IMPORT ORDER (isort)

```bash
cd ~/dutchbay-epc-model

echo "=== ISORT: FIX IMPORT ORDER ==="

.venv311/bin/python -m isort \
  --profile black \
  --recursive \
  --skip=analytics/fx/,scripts/research/,scripts/test_fx_*.py \
  analytics/ finance/ tests/ scripts/ \
  run_full_pipeline.py \
  --quiet

# Check changes
echo ""
echo "=== CHANGES FROM ISORT ==="
git diff --stat

# Show a sample of changes
git diff analytics/ finance/ tests/ scripts/ | head -50
```

**Expected:** Mostly import grouping (stdlib → third-party → local), alphabetical sort.

